{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqa12hw637x","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"resolveOwner / registry attribution: ~40% of assignee records have no session — use byWindow time-window overlap as fallback (NOT just direct + sessionTranscript)","summary":"When implementing resolveOwner(taskKey, registry): a direct-path + session-only resolver is WRONG. On real data ~40% of assignee agent records carry no session and no transcript_path, so exact-match resolution only recovers ~60% of tasks. The remaining rows are recoverable ONLY by correlating the task's claim window (registry.window[taskKey]) against harness run windows (registry.byWindow): pick the byWindow entry whose [start,end] interval overlaps the task window with the largest overlap (overlap = min(ends) - max(starts), >=0 counts as touching; missing end widens to now). Always implement all three lookups in order: (1) direct transcript_path on agent record, (2) sessionTranscript[agent.session], (3) byWindow time-window overlap correlation. CORRECT PATTERN: for (const run of registry.byWindow) { const overlap = Math.min(taskEnd, runEnd) - Math.max(taskStart, runStart); track best overlap >= 0 }. Do NOT return null after failing direct+session without attempting byWindow fallback.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-11T21:46:48.726Z","vec":[-0.08968909829854965,-0.04944932088255882,-0.027635352686047554,-0.0034358128905296326,-0.06693423539400101,0.0369483046233654,0.03797432407736778,0.036521412432193756,-0.013337405398488045,0.014936933293938637,-0.06773180514574051,-0.03568268567323685,-0.036520134657621384,0.04875299707055092,-0.002550441538915038,0.006925398949533701,0.0234299935400486,-0.058068305253982544,-0.037658628076314926,-0.07285246253013611,0.04640847072005272,-0.007856418378651142,0.0390012301504612,0.03708576783537865,-0.029585663229227066,0.019754892215132713,-0.07308778166770935,-0.09068777412176132,0.04509894922375679,0.03904333710670471,0.012811563909053802,0.0245632492